      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: the parenthetical misreads SRFI 146. The general rule is \"it is an error for any procedure defined in this SRFI to be invoked on mappings with distinct comparators, except if noted otherwise\". The only exception is `mapping\u003d?`, which must return `#f`. The comparator argument of `mapping\u003d?` and its relatives compares values, not keys, and is unrelated to the exception. The code itself is right: `%submapping?` returns `#f` for mismatched key comparators, so all five return `#f`. Something like \"(SRFI 146 excepts only `mapping\u003d?`, which returns `#f`, as its relatives here do through `%submapping?`)\" would match the SRFI.",
      "revId": "0a9ddf9aed4c8199ded78041658c37e09526b131",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
