      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T23:44:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not blocking: `mapping-catenate` is the other procedure that takes two mappings, and it still accepts mismatched comparators. `(mapping-catenate c1 (mapping c1 1 \u0027a) 2 \u0027b (mapping c2 3 \u0027c))` returns a mapping of size 3, where `c2` is a separate comparator built the same way as `c1`. By SRFI 146\u0027s general rule that call is an error. It\u0027s outside this commit\u0027s scope of set operations, so this is only a note for a follow-up.",
      "revId": "0a9ddf9aed4c8199ded78041658c37e09526b131",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
