      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T23:44:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not blocking: two side effects of checking inside the `!` forms.\n\n- The commit message says the error names the procedure, but the pure forms hand off to the `!` forms (line 458), so `(hashmap-union a d)` raises `hashmap-union!: hashmaps with different key comparators`. The same goes for `hashmap-intersection`, `-difference` and `-xor`.\n- A mismatch in a later argument is found after the earlier ones have been merged in. In `(hashmap-union! a b d)`, where only `d` has a different comparator, `a` already holds `b`\u0027s keys when the error is raised. I checked: `a` had 2 entries after the guard. That\u0027s allowed, since the call is an error, but (srfi 113) checks every argument before doing any work (`check-all-same-comparator`).\n\nFix, if wanted: check all of `rest` against `m` before the `for-each`, with the name passed in from the procedure the caller used.",
      "revId": "0a9ddf9aed4c8199ded78041658c37e09526b131",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
