      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test passes on the old code too, just slowly, so it can\u0027t catch the regression it is for.\n\nNothing in vali-test times a run, only compiles (`performance` tests). On the parent, `bag-count` took 0.27 s for 100k copies and 4.2 s for 1.6M in a debug build, growing linearly. So 10M copies is about 26 s per memory strategy, five times over, and then the test passes.\n\nCounting the predicate\u0027s calls fails on the old code and needs no big number:\n\n```scheme\n(let ((b (bag number-comparator)) (calls 0))\n  (bag-increment! b 1 1000)\n  (test 1000 (bag-count (lambda (x) (set! calls (+ calls 1)) #t) b))\n  (test 1 calls))\n```\n\nThe old fold calls the predicate 1,000 times. I ran the same probe on this patch set and it was called once.",
